  "adaptations": [
    "gen8_ggtt_invalidate is a no-op on GEN9_LP (UC GSM); the pinned gen8 mmio_invalidate_full engine invalidation is additionally run after publication and after restoration, and its completion (each control reads 0) is required.",
    "Linux only logs an invalidation timeout; this port quarantines the extent, keeps the capture and backing, and latches the publisher.",
    "gen8 clear_range is nop_clear_range in Linux (stale entries left after unbind); this port restores exactly the captured prior entries of the owned extent before invalidation.",
    "GEM_WARN_ON(GTTMMADR length != 16 MiB) is a refusal here.",
    "_wait_for_atomic spins with cpu_relax; this port pauses 1 us per tight poll and caps polls at 4096 so a stopped clock still terminates.",
    "Each entry is verified by a non-posted readback after an mfence, as the readback check named in needs_wc_ggtt_mapping's comment.",
    "Engine runtime-PM awake filtering now comes only from a required native observer bound to the held forcewake/reset/GT runtime-PM token. No producer exists yet: missing or unknown state refuses publication before PTE writes.",
    "Owner-final-release teardown captures/clears fields first; last owner release may destroy an embedded adapter."
  ],
  "not_source_derived": [
    "Requirement that GTTMMADR be a non-prefetchable 64-bit memory BAR with decode enabled (PCI semantics for registers with read side effects), not a Linux check.",
    "IOKit mapping options kIOMapAnywhere|kIOMapInhibitCache and their verification via IOMemoryMap::getMapOptions (SDK15.5 headers)."
  ],
  "xnu_source_consulted": false,
  "dependency_clearance": "A source reference is not full dependency or firmware clearance."
}
